BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Authority: Missouri Governor\nReason: July 13\, 2026 View the proclamation here . Sincerely\, OA FMDC DEATH OF SENATOR LINDSEY GRAHAM BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA A PROCLAMATION As a mark of respect for the memory and longstanding service of Senator Lindsey Graham\, I hereby order\, by the authority vested in me by the Constitution and the laws of the United States of America\, that the flag of the United States shall be flown at half-staff at the White House and upon all public buildings and grounds\, at all military \nSource: https://oa.mo.gov/facilities/facilities-operations/flag-display/flag-notifications
DTEND:20260718T230000Z
DTSTART:20260713T000000Z
SUMMARY:President Donald J. Trump has ordered the flag of the United States shall be flown at half-staff throughout the United States and its Territories and possessions immediately through Saturday\, July 18\, 2026 at 6:00 p.m.
UID:1d01ffe65d23a535cddae431f535f02a3eb6339bbb8a129f6831d5f512298c1b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Authority: Missouri Governor\nReason: Governor Mike Kehoe ordered flags to be flown at half-staff on February 28\, 2026\, to honor Deputy Sheriffs Gabriel Ramirez and Michael Hislope\, who lost their lives in the line of duty.\nSource: https://governor.mo.gov/press-releases/archive/governor-kehoe-orders-flags-fly-half-staff-honor-christian-county-deputy
DTEND:20260301T000132Z
DTSTART:20260228T124353Z
SUMMARY:Governor Kehoe orders flags to half-staff in honor of Deputy Sheriffs Ramirez and Hislope
UID:af290cd288fc65a64df82003c7b0a3c0017aac070f98d8581088b1e62b9c788c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Authority: 4 U.S.C. 7(m) and 36 U.S.C. 136\nReason: Federal law provides for the U.S. flag to be displayed at half-staff from sunrise to sunset on Peace Officers Memorial Day\, unless it falls on Armed Forces Day. The observance honors law enforcement officers who lost their lives in the line of duty and recognizes the service and sacrifice of peace officers across the country.\nSource: https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid:USC-prelim-title36-section136&num=0&edition=prelim
DTEND:20260516T011429Z
DTSTART:20260515T105822Z
SUMMARY:Peace Officers Memorial Day
UID:60263a0430f60a8ee190848f229d5e4639058081fd0525fa282660251d76a0da
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Authority: Missouri Governor\nReason: President Trump ordered all U.S. flags to half-staff to honor Dolly Parton. The order applies from August 25\, 2026 through sunset on September 1\, 2026.\nSource: https://oa.mo.gov/facilities/facilities-operations/flag-display/flag-notifications
DTEND:20260902T004107Z
DTSTART:20260826T010000Z
SUMMARY:President Trump orders flags to half-staff for Dolly Parton
UID:48d8d758587e0673aff43d67f2d69fdbe4e6a9464844f85831254e374f981b25
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Authority: US President\nReason: President Donald Trump ordered all American flags throughout the United States lowered to half-staff in honor of the life and achievements of Senator Lindsey Graham. Flags are to remain lowered until 6 p.m. on Saturday\, July 18\, 2026.\nSource: https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2026/07/death-of-senator-lindsey-graham/
DTEND:20260719T010000Z
DTSTART:20260713T003000Z
SUMMARY:President Trump orders flags to half-staff in honor of Senator Lindsey Graham
UID:8842f3fab76883193feaecee23509560f996c1898d75526a55e76965ea30a66e
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Authority: Public Law 107-51\nReason: Public Law 107-51 provides for the U.S. flag to be lowered to half-staff from sunrise to sunset for the National Fallen Firefighters Memorial Service. This observance honors firefighters who died in service to their communities and invites the country to pause in gratitude for their sacrifice.\nSource: https://www.congress.gov/107/plaws/publ51/PLAW-107publ51.pdf
DTEND:20270503T010159Z
DTSTART:20270502T111151Z
SUMMARY:National Fallen Firefighters Memorial Service
UID:217c1a119a7840d1444e72ff4d984dd3f4469bcaa32ce9015fe00db9541f0269
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Authority: 36 U.S.C. 144\nReason: Federal law requests that the U.S. flag be displayed at half-staff from sunrise to sunset on Patriot Day. The observance honors those killed in the September 11 attacks\, recognizes the bravery of responders\, and marks a national day of remembrance and resolve.\nSource: https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid:USC-prelim-title36-section144&num=0&edition=prelim
DTEND:20260912T002533Z
DTSTART:20260911T114802Z
